    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1131">

                <pb facs="0848" n="772" sameAs="frus:frus1916/pg772"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.6363/246</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Parker, representing American interests, to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mexico City</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-09-04T17:00:00-06:36">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 4, 1916, 5 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>374. Department of Hacienda to-day publishes a decree dated September 2 requiring
                    all oil compaines producing crude oil in Mexico to register in the tax bureau of
                    that Department before September 15 for companies already producing and within
                    15 days from the <pb facs="0849" n="773" xml:id="pg773"/> date of first
                    production for the companies which have not yet produced oil. This registration
                    must be made by a person duly authorized to represent the company. Failure to
                    comply may be punished by a fine of one thousand pesos Mexican gold.</p>
                <p>Text and translation will be sent by first pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Parker</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
